{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-universal-homeomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57e31add293d0c116439cb1f96779b49f7632bcbe49f668670abaf881622928a", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is a universal homeomorphism''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5589d304c66c07b5ff9e5df29dcadaceb0354c3ba9ce02a7ea4c9e05e785186a", "unit_id": "tag:0CFX:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-universally-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-base-change-surjective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-universally-injective}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-surjective}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-open}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-universal-homeomorphism}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-surjective}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-universally-injective}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-universally-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4efcb4a59056c93657f8ee5a84969388d635d1294d6bf16ac0f32729cc607d31", "source_text": "This can be proved in exactly the same manner as\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nAlternatively, one can use that a map of topological spaces is a\nhomeomorphism if and only if it is injective, surjective, and open.\nThus a universal homeomorphism is the same thing as a\nsurjective, universally injective, and universally open morphism.\nSee Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0002> and\nMorphisms of Spaces, Definitions\n<REF_0003>,\n<REF_0004>,\n<REF_0005>,\n<REF_0006>.\nThus the lemma follows from\nLemmas <REF_0007>,\n<REF_0008>, and\n<REF_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a9f2e8d1317acdeed4cd7656842b54924dd9b5b3d1e87ff27709b8c9cdd3286c", "unit_id": "tag:0CFX:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(f) =$", "MATH_0002": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descending-property-locally-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:365d02bf050f12ee9903b36c61bdf624d00b07c1586052591e25ad225aaf043e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bcffa4f35ac02327802d689c1913a229332814ea0be189730f4c7387c09b1226", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is locally of finite type''\nis fpqc local on the base.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e75122a079786b8f2da3d2079125a47b423beb08d432c41c65aa7a3107c5b911", "unit_id": "tag:041S:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$Z' \\to Z$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X \\to Z$", "MATH_0004": "$f' : Z' \\times_Z X \\to Z'$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to Z$", "MATH_0009": "$f'$", "MATH_0010": "$Z' \\times_Z U$", "MATH_0011": "$Z' \\times_Z X$", "MATH_0012": "$Z' \\times_Z U \\to Z'$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{Z' \\to Z\\}$", "MATH_0014": "$U \\to Z$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-finite-type-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-finite-type-local}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{descent-lemma-descending-property-locally-finite-type}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1bfcf741aeca8e620c1ee1f5ed7d74f26de9ede14fa1b918120f46eeef0adb84", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b1288cbb53af54bcfd28fc0c68f22c3fbdb523b8ea9d2e569b05dd040e692acd", "source_text": "We will use\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto prove this. Assumptions (1) and (2) of that lemma follow from\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a surjective flat morphism of affine schemes over <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a morphism of algebraic spaces, and assume\nthat the base change <MATH_0004> is locally of finite type.\nWe have to show that <MATH_0005> is locally of finite type. Let <MATH_0006> be a scheme\nand let <MATH_0007> be surjective and <ACCENT_0001>tale. By\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0003>\nagain, it is enough to show that <MATH_0008> is locally of finite type.\nSince <MATH_0009> is locally of finite type, and since <MATH_0010> is a\nscheme <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0011> we conclude (by the same lemma again) that\n<MATH_0012> is locally of finite type.\nAs <MATH_0013> is an fpqc covering we conclude that\n<MATH_0014> is locally of finite type by\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0004>\nas desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cb5302be91d39b727ba9669d291ac21315c95ede9252472b25e7e51a41cde332", "unit_id": "tag:041S:proof"}
